      "innovation": "Domain-specific pre-training on large-scale biomedical corpora: trains the model on clinical reports and health literacy documents to capture domain-specific context, improving upon general corpora which yield unsatisfactory results; Cross-layer parameter sharing: learns parameters for the first transformer block and reuses them in remaining layers, reducing memory consumption and increasing training speed compared to learning unique parameters per layer; Sentence Order Prediction (SOP): creates random pairs from different sentences to model inter-sentence coherence, providing a better measure of coherence loss than prior methods; Factorized embedding parameterization: decomposes the embedding matrix into two small matrices to separate hidden layer size from vocabulary embedding size, allowing larger hidden sizes without significantly increasing parameter count.",
